Third-party credit
------------------
This work is a JAX port of, and is validated against, the TOMAS (TwO-Moment
Aerosol Sectional) microphysics model. We gratefully credit:

  - The TOMAS authors, notably Peter J. Adams, John H. Seinfeld, Jeffrey R.
    Pierce and co-workers, for the TOMAS algorithms and Fortran code
    (Adams and Seinfeld, 2002, J. Geophys. Res., doi:10.1029/2001JD001010).
  - The GEOS-Chem TOMAS implementation and its developers, from which the
    TOMAS aerosol routines descend.

The Fortran source in tomas_fortran/src is a vendored copy of the original
TOMAS box-model code, included for validation benchmarks. It is redistributed
with credit to its authors and retains its original file headers and
copyright notices (including author lines and any institutional copyright
notices). Those headers must be kept intact. The vendored Fortran is NOT
licensed under the LGPL by this repository; the LGPL-3.0 above does not apply
to it, and it remains subject to whatever terms its original authors and
copyright holders set.
